---
name: Detect credential stuffing in authentication logs
description: |
  Streams the Okta System Log, normalizes it to OCSF, keeps one event per
  sign-in attempt, detects sources that fail logons across many accounts, and
  sends the OCSF Detection Findings to
  Splunk.
---

okta::fetch "example.okta.com", bearer_token=secret("okta-bearer-token")
okta::ocsf::normalize
// Okta logs several Authentication events per sign-in. Keep only the session
// start, which records the outcome of the credential check once per attempt.
where metadata.event_code == "user.session.start"
tenzir::detect::authentication::credential_stuffing
to_splunk "https://splunk.example.com:8088", hec_token=secret("splunk-hec-token")
